# POS → Priority automation — cancel test documents

Applies to any test run of the n8n workflow **"Point Of Sale v6 - Main Scenarios"** (`qqvFgOV6PhNV3AyK`, webhook `Main Creator`) or anything else that creates documents in Priority (`https://carpetshop.wee.co.il/odata/Priority/tabula.ini/a051118`).

## Rule

Every document a test creates must be **PATCHed to status `מבוטלת`** in the same session, right after verifying the run. Do not leave test drafts for the operator to delete.

1. Read the created document numbers from the execution (`סיכום` node: `ordName`, `einvoiceIvnum`, `receiptIvnum`, `rentalDocNo`) — including partial runs that failed mid-way (take the number from the error response).
2. PATCH each one to `מבוטלת`:

| Document | Entity key | Status field |
|---|---|---|
| Order | `ORDERS('<ORDNAME>')` | `ORDSTATUSDES` |
| חשבונית מס קבלה | `EINVOICES(IVNUM='<IVNUM>',IVTYPE='E',DEBIT='D')` | `STATDES` |
| Receipt | `TINVOICES(IVNUM='<IVNUM>',IVTYPE='T',DEBIT='D')` | `STATDES` |
| Rental | `DOCUMENTS_D(DOCNO='<DOCNO>',TYPE='D')` | `STATDES` |

   Confirm the entity key format with a GET before the first PATCH; if it differs, fix this table.
3. Read each document back and confirm the status is `מבוטלת`. If Priority refuses (e.g. document already closed), report the number to the operator — never silently skip.

## Test constraints (still apply)

- Customer phone stays `0547495083` (keeps documents as טיוטא); use fresh `POS-<n>` order ids.
- Use the existing Priority credential (`Carpetshop's Priority API`) — no new credentials.
- No bank-transfer live tests without asking (they email accounting).
